Goal: close the pinned Java 5.5.1 public `MQHelper` timestamp-reset API slice
within Phase 18, on branch `phase/18-phase-18-compatibility-closure`.

Pinned source: `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`,
`client/src/main/java/org/apache/rocketmq/client/MQHelper.java`.

Changes:
- Added `MqHelper::reset_offset_by_timestamp` for Java's deprecated overload;
  it selects instance `DEFAULT`.
- Added `reset_offset_by_timestamp_with_instance`, which creates and starts a
  Pull consumer, traverses queues in `MessageQueue`/Java `TreeSet` order,
  searches the lower timestamp bound, applies nonnegative results, persists the
  fetched queue set, and shuts down after the operation.
- Re-exported `MqHelper` from the consumer crate and top-level facade.
- Pinned both Java overloads in the consumer facade reflection fixture and
  recorded the Rust mapping in the Phase 10 and Java 5.5.1 compatibility
  inventories.

Verification passed:
- `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-consumer --all-features --locked`
  (239 unit tests, all integration targets, 13 doctests).
- `cargo clippy -p rocketmq-classic-consumer --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings`
- `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic --test facade_public_types --locked`
- `mvn -q -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml exec:java@verify-consumer-facade-api-fixture`
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check`
- `git diff --check`

Fixture: `fixtures/consumer/facade-api.json`, SHA-256
`6d38837ca80e7012a35069800144888fa0980c5e2783785b7e998c1d2efa2b1c`.

This closes only the MQHelper utility API slice. Broad P18-V01
